jz-dtrng: take IRQ_DTRNG from the T41 dt-bindings header

T40 already gets its interrupt number from
<dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/t40-irq.h>; every other SoC falls
through to <soc/irq.h>. That header does not exist for T41 - and in fact
does not exist for T40 either, which is why T40 has its own branch. The
XBurst2 SoC include directories only carry include/irq.h, not
include/soc/irq.h. So a T41 build stops at:

    jz-dtrng.c:31:10: fatal error: soc/irq.h: No such file or directory

T41 has the same dt-bindings header, and it defines IRQ_DTRNG, so give
T41 the same branch T40 has. Other SoCs are untouched.

Upstream: https://github.com/openipc/openingenic

Signed-off-by: Oskari Rauta <oskari.rauta@gmail.com>

diff --git a/kernel/misc/jz-dtrng/jz-dtrng.c b/kernel/misc/jz-dtrng/jz-dtrng.c
index 4323742..e9c3df5 100644
--- a/kernel/misc/jz-dtrng/jz-dtrng.c
+++ b/kernel/misc/jz-dtrng/jz-dtrng.c
@@ -27,6 +27,8 @@
 #include <soc/base.h>
 #ifdef CONFIG_SOC_T40
 #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/t40-irq.h>
+#elif defined(CONFIG_SOC_T41)
+#include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/t41-irq.h>
 #else
 #include <soc/irq.h>
 #endif
